---
description: Observe customer problem episodes, count independent incident events, maintain stable mechanism concepts, and report only comparable population trends.
args: { question: ObservatoryQuestion, observations: SignalObservationSet, prior?: ObservatoryCheckpoint | null }
returns: ObservatoryRun
uses: [customerObservatory/assembleRequest, customerObservatory/assembleDossier, customerObservatory/frameObservatoryQuestion, customerObservatory/extractCustomerSituations, customerObservatory/versionCustomerIdentity, customerObservatory/deduplicateIncidentEvents, customerObservatory/versionProblemConcepts, customerObservatory/revokeAttributionDerivatives, customerObservatory/compareTrendCoverage, customerObservatory/bindTrendAggregates, customerObservatory/commissionDiscriminatingInvestigation, customerObservatory/compareObservatoryRevisions, customerObservatory/reconcileObservatoryCheckpoint]
---
Bind saved = prior when supplied, otherwise null. Treat null as a first run; preserve all original task and evidence inputs.
1. Bind request = assembleRequest(question) and dossier = assembleDossier(observations). Preserve the question's original time window and population; do not infer omitted source categories or receipts. A prior checkpoint belongs to this observatory case; do not reuse it for another case.
2. Bind frame = frameObservatoryQuestion(request, dossier.studies). Freeze population definition, observation window, question and study version.
3. Bind episodes = extractCustomerSituations(request, dossier.rawEpisodes, dossier.evidencePages). Preserve raw source IDs and separate requested features from experienced problems.
4. Bind identityLedger = versionCustomerIdentity(episodes, dossier.identityMapVersions) before any customer counts. Migration joins require a versioned identity map; unresolved IDs block affected denominators.
5. Bind consentPlan = revokeAttributionDerivatives(episodes, dossier.consentChanges) before selecting public quotations. Withdrawn attribution requires removal and recomputation proposals; non-attributable incident evidence remains with its provenance.
6. Bind incidents = deduplicateIncidentEvents(episodes, identityLedger, dossier.outageReceipts). Collapse copied messages and outage tickets as one event volume, while retaining actual repeat failures on separate occasions.
7. Bind problemMap = versionProblemConcepts(incidents, dossier.conceptRenameEvents, dossier.evidencePages). Keep concept IDs stable across renames and inspect counterexamples before moving episodes.
8. Bind trendCoverage = compareTrendCoverage(request, dossier.samplingFrames, identityLedger, dossier.trendReceipts). A disappearing channel, incomplete sample or unresolved migration breaks comparability and forbids improvement claims.
9. Bind trends = bindTrendAggregates(request, problemMap, trendCoverage, dossier.trendReceipts) only when exact receipts exist and coverage is comparable; otherwise preserve the unavailable trend state without inventing a count.
10. Bind investigations = commissionDiscriminatingInvestigation(request, problemMap, trends, dossier.evidencePages). Select mechanism uncertainty that could change a product decision and cite both evidence directions.
11. Bind invalidations = compareObservatoryRevisions(saved, request, frame, episodes, identityLedger, incidents, problemMap, trends, consentPlan). Revoke only derivative IDs whose consent, identity, event grouping or concept lineage changed; keep unaffected trend windows and prior investigations available.
12. Bind checkpoint = reconcileObservatoryCheckpoint(saved, request, dossier, episodes, identityLedger, incidents, problemMap, trends, investigations, consentPlan, invalidations). Append new source-version findings by stable identity, preserve superseded editions, and treat identical source snapshot replay as a no-op. A snapshot change is not evidence that prior counts or deletion effects were committed.
13. Return { caseId: request.caseId, checkpoint, frame, episodes, identityLedger, consentPlan, incidents, problemMap, trends, investigations, invalidations, outstandingEffects: invalidations.unresolvedDeletionReceiptIds plus consentPlan.derivedArtifactsToRecompute plus identityLedger.countsBlockedUntilVersioned, commitAllowed: false } as ObservatoryRun. Counts and external deletion effects require actual typed service receipts; a checkpoint records analysis state, not those effects.
